    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** (75.66) and **Mickey Moniak** (72.51) serving as our primary offensive engines. **Corbin Carroll** is our clear top play; despite facing an elite arm in Trevor McDonald, the projection model loves his ability to exploit the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery for stolen base opportunities, which remain our highest-weighted priority. Meanwhile, **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a massive park-factor boost and a favorable platoon matchup against Max Meyer, allowing his efficiency to soar despite a tough assignment. We also see high-floor reliability from **Brice Turang** (67.08) and **James Wood** (64.98), both of whom provide essential stability as we manage our daily game caps.\n\nThe optimization process faced its most difficult decision at the final utility spot, where **Kyle Karros** (44.93) narrowly missed the cut. While **Kyle Karros** benefits from the same park factors as **Mickey Moniak**, his projected efficiency was suppressed by a poor slot in the batting order and the inherent risk of facing Max Meyer, leaving him just shy of our \"Strong\" tier. Additionally, we are monitoring \"Lineup Pending\" statuses for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, **Max Muncy**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Corbin Carroll**. Should official lineups shift these players into bottom-third slots, we may see further degradation in their expected output. While **Seiya Suzuki** (60.27) sits safely in the lineup, we are keeping a close eye on wind conditions, as the projected outflow provides a marginal, yet welcome, boost to his power potential against a formidable arm like Buehler.",
